// Unshielded token types this environment's chain holds, aggregated over the block
// range the scanner covered. Generated by qa/tools/block-scanner: the unshielded
// UTXOs of the scanned blocks are grouped by token type and owner, keeping the ones
// still unspent.
//
// The custom (non-NIGHT) entries are what this file exists for: the custom
// unshielded token e2e suite needs a token the funding wallet can actually spend,
// and no chain has one from genesis — it has to be minted by a contract.
//
// CANDIDATES, NOT GUARANTEES: "unspent" is point-in-time. A UTXO recorded here can
// be spent right after the scan, and holdings created outside the scanned range are
// not seen at all. Consumers must probe the live balance and skip when it is gone —
// which is why several candidates are recorded rather than one.
//
// The holders are recorded for human review only — no test reads them. On a QA
// environment the holder of a custom token is normally the environment's funding wallet
// by construction, since the token is minted into it for the e2e suite to spend; the
// address and its balances are public on-chain data either way.
//
// Re-run `bun run generate:data` (see qa/tools/block-scanner/README.md) to refresh.
{
  // Heights of the first and last transaction-carrying block of the scan, and the
  // moment the scan ran: the point in time the "unspent" values refer to.
  "scan": {
    "from-block": 14708,
    "to-block": 233106,
    "scanned-at": "2026-08-10T20:22:21.377Z"
  },
  // NIGHT (the all-zero token type) is on every chain and dominates every scan, so
  // it is summarised here instead of being listed as a candidate. Zero means the
  // scan saw no unshielded activity at all, not that NIGHT is absent.
  "night": {
    "unspent-utxos": 83894,
    "distinct-owners": 543
  },
  // Custom token types, best candidate first (largest single-owner unspent value).
  "custom-tokens": [
    {
      "token-type": "27b7cfdff3d67408890de83ab711d0066cd89b436b15a5723bc21aed82a74130",
      "unspent-holders": [
        {
